<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">21 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 21 April, from 753 BCE to 1960.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/romulus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/romulus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">753 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,778 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Romulus founds Rome, according to Roman tradition</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Roman writers placed the city's foundation by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus">Romulus</a> on the Palatine on 21 April 753 BCE, a date fixed by the scholar Varro. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> celebrated it each year as the Parilia.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/43-bce">43 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,068 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mark Antony fights Senate forces at the Battle of Mutina</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Mutina</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cisalpine-gaul">Cisalpine Gaul</a>, Senate forces under the consuls Pansa and Hirtius, with Octavian, fought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a>, who was besieging Caesar's assassin Decimus Brutus there. Brutus was relieved, but later deserted by his troops and killed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mark-antony">Mark Antony</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/decimus-junius-brutus-albinus">Decimus Junius Brutus Albinus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/900">900 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,126 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A debt pardon is recorded on the Laguna Copperplate Inscription</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> plate dated to the Saka year 822 recorded the cancellation of a debt and named a leader of Tundun, usually identified with Tondo on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luzon">Luzon</a>. Found in 1989, it is the oldest known document from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laguna-copperplate-inscription">Laguna Copperplate Inscription</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luzon">Luzon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1092">1092 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">934 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Urban II raises Pisa to an archdiocese</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-urban-ii">Pope Urban II</a> elevated the Diocese of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pisa">Pisa</a>, founded in the 4th century, to the dignity of a metropolitan archdiocese, with its seat in the cathedral of the Assumption.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-urban-ii">Pope Urban II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1506">1506 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">520 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Three days of massacre in Lisbon come to an end</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Rioting stirred up by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-order">Dominican friars</a> killed between 1,000 and 4,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-christians">New Christians</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> forcibly converted in 1497. King Manuel I punished the city and had two of the friars executed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-christians">New Christians</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1782">1782 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">244 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rama I founds Bangkok as Siam's new capital</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The city pillar of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangkok">Bangkok</a> was erected on the east bank of the Chao Phraya, marking the official founding of the new royal capital. It replaced Thonburi across the river.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1836">1836 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">190 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Texans defeat Santa Anna at San Jacinto</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sam-houston">Sam Houston</a>'s army surprised the Mexican camp and won in about eighteen minutes. Santa Anna was captured the next day and forced to order his troops out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>, securing its independence.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1918">1918 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Red Baron is shot down and killed near Amiens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Manfred von Richthofen, credited with 80 victories, was killed while pursuing an enemy aircraft over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somme-river">Somme</a>. Whether a Canadian pilot or Australian ground gunners fired the fatal shot is still debated.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1960">1960 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">66 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Brasília is inaugurated as Brazil's capital</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Built in under four years to plans by Lúcio Costa and Oscar Niemeyer, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brasilia">Brasília</a> replaced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a> as capital. It was meant to draw development into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>'s interior.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 21 April <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sancho-vi-of-navarre"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sancho-vi-of-navarre.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sancho VI of Navarre</span><span class="tp">1132–1194</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/marco-antonio-bragadin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/marco-antonio-bragadin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Marco Antonio Bragadin</span><span class="tp">1523–1571</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jan-van-riebeeck"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jan-van-riebeeck.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jan van Riebeeck</span><span class="tp">1619–1677</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/elizabeth-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/elizabeth-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Elizabeth II</span><span class="tp">1926–2022</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 21 April <span class="n">12</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emperor-xian-of-han"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emperor-xian-of-han.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emperor Xian of Han</span><span class="tp">181–234</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/anselm-of-canterbury"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/anselm-of-canterbury.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Anselm of Canterbury</span><span class="tp">c. 1033–1109</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/marie-of-montpellier"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/marie-of-montpellier.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Marie of Montpellier</span><span class="tp">c. 1182–1213</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-vii-of-england"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-vii-of-england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henry VII of England</span><span class="tp">1457–1509</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/cosimo-i-de-medici"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/cosimo-i-de-medici.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Cosimo I de' Medici</span><span class="tp">1519–1574</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sen-no-rikyu"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sen-no-rikyu.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sen no Rikyū</span><span class="tp">1522–1591</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/prince-eugene-of-savoy"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/prince-eugene-of-savoy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Prince Eugene of Savoy</span><span class="tp">1663–1736</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mark-twain"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mark-twain.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mark Twain</span><span class="tp">1835–1910</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-maynard-keynes"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-maynard-keynes.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Maynard Keynes</span><span class="tp">1883–1946</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francois-duvalier"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francois-duvalier.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">François Duvalier</span><span class="tp">1907–1971</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tancredo-neves"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tancredo-neves.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Tancredo Neves</span><span class="tp">1910–1985</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-francis"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-francis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Francis</span><span class="tp">1936–2025</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
